This product uses public amateur-radio reference data supplied by its configured
sources. Those datasets remain subject to their respective providers' terms.

The OM0RX-xLog icon was created specifically for this project.

The isolated integration prototype includes pure-domain code adapted from
OM0RX-xCluster by Oliver Bross OM0RX, GPL-3.0-only, source revision
776b7b04ffa5a9057f1e909339393549a103836b. Exact file provenance and deliberate
changes are recorded in docs/P2_CLUSTER_PROVENANCE.md.
The new station contracts preserve observed-state requirements from OM0RX-xCat
and xLog; their provenance and unintegrated boundaries are recorded in
docs/P2_STATION_CONTRACT.md. Existing standalone applications remain preserved.

The Mac direct-station integration includes a byte-identical snapshot of
OM0RX-xCat XCatCore by Oliver Bross OM0RX, GPL-3.0-only. Its exact source
revision, local worktree-diff fingerprint, and file hashes are recorded in
docs/XCAT_INTEGRATION_PROVENANCE.md. The original xCat checkout remains untouched.

The read-only chaser and DX calendar are independently implemented from the
ShackCQ GPL-3.0-only behavioral contracts at the pinned revision in
docs/OPPORTUNITIES_PROVENANCE.md. Public spot publishers and 425DXN retain
their own data terms and visible source attribution. No third-party calendar
code or raw provider data is bundled.

The initial CQ WW CW and CQ WPX CW contest-rule and Cabrillo QSO-layout behavior
in Sources/XContestCore/PilotRules.swift and Sources/XContestCore/Cabrillo.swift
is a Swift translation adapted from
Not1MM by Michael Bridak (GPL-3.0-or-later), using Oliver Bross's read-only
contest-sw fork at revision 7c8b499225a73f7f8f792246881bd7aefc05452f.
The translated source paths are not1mm/plugins/cq_ww_cw.py,
not1mm/plugins/cq_wpx_cw.py, not1mm/lib/ham_utility.py,
not1mm/lib/database.py and duplicate dispatch in not1mm/__main__.py. The
translation was modified for OM0RX-xLog on 17 October 2026; exact behavioral
scope and differences are recorded in docs/contesting/CORE_CONTRACT.md.
